    "id": "y0puzFLSmQqBjOJzXez9",
    "description": "These traveler’s provisions vary from region to region. In the Blazing Garden they’ll include monster jerky but in the Twilight Meridian it’ll be dried seaweeds.\n- 1 Ration provides 1 day’s nutrition."
  },
  {
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Holy Icon",
    "creator": "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2",
    "type": "none",
    "actions": [],
    "uses": {
      "max": 0
    },
    "privacy": {
      "users": [
        "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2"
      ],
      "level": "private"
    },
    "id": "4jUbCzSGG4BUuKg8xMy4",
    "description": "Holy Icons are objects that allow mortals to focus their faith to briefly repel unearthly creatures. These can be holy symbols, but also items loaded with sentiment or meaning. For example, sacred prayer chains or a childhood toy.\n\nYou can use your Action to boldly present your Holy Icon in an attempt to ward off Asura, Devas, Undead, Unshaped, or any creature with 4 or more Bright or Dark Allegiance Points.\n\n**Requires an Aura Contest**\n- **Success:** The unearthly one cannot direct an Attack at you as long as you continue presenting your Icon.\n- **Failure:** They laugh at your pathetic gesture. You cannot attempt to repel them again for 24 hours.\n- Your GM may render an Icon ineffective when held by someone who does not believe strongly in what the Icon represents.",
    "data": {
      "cost": {
        "coins": 75
      },
      "subtype": "curiosities, artifacts, & gadgets",
      "encumbrance": 1,
      "type": "Gear"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "This gadget allows you to perform crude manual manipulation from a safe distance. The Grabber is composed of a telescoping pole with a mechanical gauntlet affixed to one end and controls at the other.\n\n- The Grabber enables you to grasp, poke, or push an object up to 10 ft away, or 1 Battlefield Area.\n- The shaft of the Grabber can be extended and retracted rapidly, allowing you to yoink an object. During a Fight, this requires the use of your Action.\n- Precise tasks requiring fine motor skills are not possible. However, your GM may allow you to perform more difficult manoeuvres with a Deftness Check.",
    "data": {
      "encumbrance": 2,
      "type": "Gear",
      "cost": {
        "coins": 45
      },
      "subtype": "curiosities, artifacts, & gadgets"
    },
    "creator": "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2",
