  {
    "creator": "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2",
    "type": "none",
    "id": "XE4FWvCEGWdRgyp8Jdn6",
    "actions": [],
    "uses": {
      "max": 0
    },
    "privacy": {
      "level": "private",
      "users": [
        "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2"
      ]
    },
    "description": "Combination merges the benefits of two Weapon Types, making them difficult and expensive to forge. Combination Weapons inherit the properties of their two constituent weapons in the following way:\n  - The Weapon Abilities of both.\n  - The usage restrictions of both.\n  - Take up the Inventory Slots from the largest of the two weapons.\n  - The Extra Damage of the most effective weapon.\n\nFor example, a Master-Arc Combination Weapon would gain a +1 to Attack rolls (Master), be able to target two foes in the same area (Arc), require both hands to use without penalty (Arc), and take up 3 Inventory Slots (Arc).\n\n- If any Missile and Melee Weapon Types are combined, you must choose which mode of attack you are using for your Action (i.e Melee or Missile).\n- These weapons only benefit from Missile Weapon Abilities when making Missile attacks.\n- These weapons only benefit from Melee Weapon Abilities when making Melee attacks.\n- The Extra Damage value used is taken from the base weapon appropriate to your chosen mode of attack.\n- Concealed and Thrown Weapons can only be combined with each other, due to their small size.\n- Combining two weapons that each have an inherent **Weapon Ability** will take you to the 3 Ability limit. Your GM may deem some combinations impossible. Common sense should be the guide.\n\n**Coins** = (Price of Weapon Type 1 + Weapon Type 2) x2",
    "data": {
      "subtype": "weapons",
      "type": "Gear"
    },
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Weapon Ability - Combination"
  },
  {
    "description": "While all weapons are inherently harmful, these weapons are made to inflict maximum damage at the expense of the wielders safety. \n- Available for Melee Weapons only. \n-  This weapons threshold to deal Extra Damage is lowered by 2. \n- You take 1 Heart of Damage whenever you get an unmodified 1 or 2 on your Attack roll.\n\n**Coins** = Weapon Price + -10",
    "data": {
      "type": "Gear",
      "subtype": "weapons"
    },
    "creator": "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2",
    "type": "none",
    "id": "hVlU17YlkhlpHLZT6fIW",
