    "actions": [],
    "id": "TXuMXlNnQDDg97hfiSic",
    "creator": "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2",
    "type": "none",
    "data": {
      "subtype": "weapons",
      "type": "Gear"
    },
    "description": "Special Ammunition provides ranged weapons with more tactical options. It enables you to create distractions, signal for help, or simply do more harm. \n\n- Available for Missile Weapons only.\n- **Fireberry Shot:** These do Flame Damage instead of Mundane Damage. Your GM may also allow other types of Special Damage .\n- **Flare:** Ammunition that creates a lingering and visually impressive effect, such as bright light, when shot. Ineffective as a weapon but a good signal.\n- **Heavy:** A large, clumsy shot that incurs a Major Penalty (-4) on your Attack roll when used, but does +1 Heart of Damage on a successful hit.\n- **Whistling:** Ammunition that makes an ear-splitting scream when fired. Anyone in earshot must make a successful Insight Check or be Deafened  on their next Turn. Just like regular ammunition, these variants are expended after use.\n\n**Coins** = Ammo Price x2",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Weapon Ability - Special Ammunition"
  },
  {
    "name": "Weapon Ability - Utility",
    "version": 1,
    "id": "dtwF5RfUbFzctrHAHAEG",
    "privacy": {
      "users": [
        "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2"
      ],
      "level": "private"
    },
    "uses": {
      "max": 0
    },
    "actions": [],
    "type": "none",
    "creator": "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2",
    "data": {
      "subtype": "weapons",
      "type": "Gear"
    },
    "description": "This allows a weapon to also function as a simple tool. For example, a Fishing Rod Spear or a Shovel Sword. \n\n- You can combine a weapon with a tool that falls under Adventuring Gear, Common Rural Goods, Common Urban Goods, or Oddities & Luxury Items. \n- Utility weapons take up as many Inventory Slots as the largest of their two components. \n- Your GM may deem some combinations impossible. Common sense should be the guide.\n\n**Coins** = Weapon Price + Tool Price +5"
  }
]